  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-15) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=3\\,\\text{s},$ we substitute $t=3$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(3) & =3(3)^{2}-2(3) \\\\  & =27-6 \\\\  & =21\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
